---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';
const path = '/compare/yotpo-email-sms-vs-postscript';
const title = 'Yotpo Email & SMS vs Postscript for Shopify: 2026 Comparison';
const desc = "Yotpo Email & SMS is retired. Move the SMS program while deciding where email belongs.";
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Can I choose Yotpo Email & SMS today?",
    "answer": "Yotpo states that the application is decommissioned. This is now a migration decision, separate from retaining its Reviews or Loyalty products."
  },
  {
    "question": "Is Postscript still SMS only?",
    "answer": "No. Its current product pages advertise Postscript Email. Evaluate its present capabilities rather than relying on an older SMS-only description."
  },
  {
    "question": "Will importing subscribers transfer my phone number?",
    "answer": "Treat subscriber import and number provisioning or transfer as separate tasks. Confirm the path and readiness with the receiving provider before scheduling sends."
  },
  {
    "question": "Can I keep Yotpo loyalty data?",
    "answer": "Postscript documents a Yotpo integration for reward points. Check the fields and behavior in your account; do not infer that every review or loyalty workflow is included."
  },
  {
    "question": "Can I export from the retired account now?",
    "answer": "Do not assume access remains available. Use records already retained and ask the relevant support teams about missing data; this page promises no recovery or export access."
  },
  {
    "question": "Should I also evaluate Sequenzy?",
    "answer": "You can include Sequenzy in the email shortlist. Verify the required Shopify events, suppression, consent handling and current commercial terms before choosing it; it is not assumed to replace SMS or review infrastructure."
  }
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />

  <section class="py-14 md:py-20">
    <div class="container">
      <nav class="mb-8 text-sm">
        <a class="link" href="/compare">Comparisons</a>
        <span class="mx-2 text-cyan-100/90">/</span>
        <span class="text-cyan-100/90">Yotpo Email & SMS vs Postscript</span>
      </nav>

      <header class="max-w-4xl">
        <p class="badge">Migration comparison · reviewed November 24, 2026</p>
        <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">Yotpo Email &amp; SMS vs Postscript for Shopify</h1>
        <p class="mt-7 text-xl leading-9">Move the SMS program while deciding where email belongs. Yotpo confirms that Email &amp; SMS has been decommissioned. This page evaluates a replacement workflow, not a trial of two currently available senders.</p>
      </header>
      <article class="prose-shopify mt-14 max-w-4xl">
        <h2>Current scope includes email</h2>
        <p>Postscript now advertises an email product. The old claim that it cannot cover email is obsolete. That does not establish feature parity with every former Yotpo flow: evaluate the current email product against your required triggers, content, reporting and suppression. You can also retain a separate email owner if that better fits the program.</p>
        <h2>Subscriber evidence comes before a broadcast</h2>
        <p>Postscript publishes a Yotpo/SMSBump migration guide for previously collected subscriber lists. Reconcile the files already retained against opt-outs and source records. A customer phone field is not enough to establish that the person belongs on a marketing list. Historical export instructions do not guarantee access to the decommissioned Yotpo application now.</p>
        <h2>Number transfer and sender change are different projects</h2>
        <p>The Yotpo migration page discusses dedicated short codes and toll-free numbers. Ask the receiving team to confirm the actual number path and readiness before scheduling a release. Record whether the sender changes, who handles replies during the handoff and what happens to pending messages. Do not assume an imported list also transfers a number or conversation history.</p>
        <h2>Proposed restock and reply acceptance scenario</h2>
        <p>For a hypothetical supplement restock, use controlled recipients to check a permitted subscriber, an opted-out subscriber, a recent purchaser and an incoming product question. Confirm exclusions and reply ownership before considering a larger broadcast. Route health-related questions to trained support using approved product information; a marketing automation should not improvise dosing advice.</p>
        <h2>Reward points and review requests need separate checks</h2>
        <p>Postscript documents a Yotpo integration for referencing reward points in SMS automations. Validate the actual balance and missing-data behavior before promising a reward. This is not proof that review eligibility, images or every loyalty event transfers. Assign review invitations to one owner and coordinate them with any restock promotion.</p>
        <h2>Budget the message actually sent</h2>
        <p>Request a quote using destination mix, message format, segment count and anticipated cadence, including carrier and number-related charges where applicable. A photo-led MMS and a short text should not be modeled as interchangeable. Compare margin after product cost, discount and messaging expense; attributed sales alone cannot establish profitable incremental demand.</p>
        <h2>Where Sequenzy fits</h2>
        <p>If you are considering Sequenzy for email, compare the same required events, exclusions and operating tasks before selecting it. Confirm current Shopify integration scope and pricing directly. Do not assume it replaces the SMS sender, review collection or loyalty service.</p>
        <h2>Primary evidence and limits</h2>
        <p>Supplier documentation checked November 24, 2026. No live migration, deliverability experiment or merchant revenue test was performed. Current account eligibility, quotes and missing historical records remain to be confirmed.</p>
        <ul>
          <li><a class="link" href="https://email-and-sms.yotpo.com/">Yotpo decommissioning notice</a></li>
          <li><a class="link" href="https://postscript.io/launch">Postscript current product releases</a></li>
          <li><a class="link" href="https://help.postscript.io/en/articles/13563834-migrating-from-yotpo-smsbump-to-postscript">Postscript Yotpo migration guide</a></li>
          <li><a class="link" href="https://help.postscript.io/en/articles/13564274-set-up-your-yotpo-integration">Postscript Yotpo rewards integration</a></li>
          <li><a class="link" href="https://postscript.io/yotpo-self-serve">Postscript sender-number guidance</a></li>
        </ul>
      </article>
      <div class="mt-10 max-w-4xl text-sm">
        <p class="font-black text-white">Related comparisons</p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          <a class="link" href="/compare/klaviyo-vs-postscript">Klaviyo vs Postscript</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/omnisend-vs-postscript">Omnisend vs Postscript</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/postscript-vs-attentive">Postscript vs Attentive</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/for/supplements">Email apps for supplement stores</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/use-cases/abandoned-cart">Abandoned cart playbook</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Yotpo Email &amp; SMS vs Postscript FAQ" />
</BaseLayout>
